why Your own pet at 10: three practice tames with a Taming Rod teach Tame Beast, then Beast Training.

# The Alliance hunter pet chains, one per home: Humans with Josephine Carson
# in Goldshire (Forever-new: 94792, 94863, 94864, then Training the Beast
# 94793 to Isaac Chan beside her), Dwarves with Grif Wildheart in Kharanos
# (6064, 6084, 6085, then 6086 to Belia Thundergranite in Ironforge), Night
# Elves with Dazalar in Dolanaar (6063, 6101, 6102, then 6103 to Jocaste in
# Darnassus), Skyborne with Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar on Zephras Isle
# (Forever-new: 94978, 94979, 94013, then 94050 to Quel'dora Quickgale;
# Elayaa Easewind's breadcrumb 94007 points there).
# Josephine's chain is open to Human, Dwarf, Night Elf, Gnome and Skyborne
# (Forever's quest data; Gnomes cannot be hunters), so a Dwarf or Night Elf
# who is in Elwynn at 10, or a Skyborne who left Zephras Isle without taming,
# can do it there instead; the guide offers it to Skyborne only when the
# Zephras chain is not done. The Goldshire steps come last; after the first
# accept they carry no race filter but `when !turnedin 6064/6063`, and the
# Dwarf and Night Elf steps carry `when` lines that close once Josephine's
# chain is taken, so a Dwarf or Night Elf who takes her rod is led through
# Goldshire instead of being held at Grif or Dazalar.
# The Hunter's Path breadcrumbs (6071-6073, 6721, 6722 to Dazalar; 6074-6076
# to Grif) are optional: the taming givers hand out the first rod without
# them, and only one of each set can be done.
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json, items.json for givers, rods, beasts and
# places; quest-notes/quest-mechanics for beast levels, respawns, the channel,
# the rod's charges and the beasts' abilities; Forever's Hunter class quest
# list: Training the Beast now teaches Beast Training (no Training Lesson);
# the card's spells (Tame Beast 1515, Beast Training 5149) from the class
# reward table.
# The leveling routes (alliance/human/01-elwynn-forest, dwarf-gnome/
# 01-dun-morogh, nightelf/01-teldrassil, skyborne/01-zephras-isle) do these
# chains on the way; this guide is for anyone off the route and adds the pet
# basics. Pet basics are Classic rules that a Forever hunter community wiki
# lists unchanged.
# Checked against Forever: Blizzard's beta development notes fix pet happiness
# at max loyalty (so happiness and loyalty are in the game), and a Forever
# hunter pet guide from beta play gives happiness at 125/100/75% damage, six
# loyalty ranks and 300 training points at 60 Best Friend, the Classic formula
# (pet level x (loyalty - 1)).
# ASSUMED: a hunter who finished one taming chain is not offered Josephine Carson's as well (Forever's data marks no exclusion between them). In-game check: does Josephine offer Taming the Beast to a Skyborne or Night Elf hunter who already knows Tame Beast?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skyborne: Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar

step Elayaa Easewind
  only Skyborne
  zone Zephras Isle
  skipto goldshire when !zone "Zephras Isle"
  tip At 10, Elayaa Easewind, a hunter trainer on Zephras Isle, may send you on to Valanaar with Taming the Beast. It is only a pointer: skip it if you are already in Valanaar.
  level 10
  accept 94007 optional                       -- Elayaa Easewind

step Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar
  only Skyborne
  tip Quel'ana Quickgale stands with the trainers by Valanaar's west gate, Quel'dora Quickgale beside her.
  turnin 94007 optional                       -- Quel'ana Quickgale
  accept 94978                                -- Quel'ana Quickgale: the first Taming Rod

step Windsong Crawler
  only Skyborne
  tip Windsong Crawlers live only by water: the nearest scuttle along the shore south-west of Valanaar, among the crabs. How the rod works: target a living crawler, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you; moving, fighting back or anyone else's help breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges. Killing one does not count. Keep each rod: it goes back to Quel'ana.
  kill 254588 quest 94978.1 "Tame Windsong Crawler" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living crawler
  turnin 94978                                -- Quel'ana Quickgale
  accept 94979

step Ornery Galestrider
  only Skyborne
  tip Dismiss the crawler first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet). Ornery Galestriders graze in the Gustberry Lowlands, the fields a short walk west and south-west of Valanaar.
  kill 251707 quest 94979.1 "Tame Ornery Galestrider" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living galestrider
  turnin 94979                                -- Quel'ana Quickgale
  accept 94013

step Vuldren Alpha
  only Skyborne
  tip Dismiss the galestrider. Vuldren Alphas hunt in the same Gustberry Lowlands, a little further south.
  kill 250874 quest 94013.1 "Tame Vuldren Alpha" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living alpha
  turnin 94013                                -- Quel'ana Quickgale: Tame Beast
  accept 94050
  turnin 94050                                -- Quel'dora Quickgale, beside her: Beast Training

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Dwarf: Grif Wildheart in Kharanos

step Grif Wildheart in Kharanos
  only Dwarf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip At 10 go to Grif Wildheart, the hunter trainer at the smithy in Kharanos. The Hunter's Path from Olmin Burningbeard in Ironforge, Tristane Shadowstone north-west of Kharanos or Einris Brightspear in Stormwind also leads here, for a little experience; it is only a pointer. In Elwynn at 10 instead? Josephine Carson's chain in Goldshire teaches the same.
  level 10
  accept 6064                                 -- Grif Wildheart: the first Taming Rod

step Large Crag Boar
  only Dwarf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  tip Large Crag Boars (level 6-7) root around the fields west, south and north-west of Kharanos and respawn every 3 minutes. How the rod works: target a living beast, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you. Moving, fighting back, being out of range or anyone else's help breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges; if they run out, destroy the rod, abandon the quest and take it again from Grif. The boars use Rushing Charge from 25 yards, so start with the rod, not Auto Shot. Keep each rod: it goes back to Grif.
  kill 1126 quest 6064.1 "Tame Large Crag Boar" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living boar
  turnin 6064                                 -- Grif Wildheart
  accept 6084

step Snow Leopard
  only Dwarf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  tip Dismiss the boar first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet): a released practice pet can turn on you. Snow Leopards (level 7-8) prowl the slopes south-east of Kharanos, more north-west and west of it; the smaller Juvenile Snow Leopards do not count.
  kill 1201 quest 6084.1 "Tame Snow Leopard" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living leopard
  turnin 6084                                 -- Grif Wildheart
  accept 6085

step Ice Claw Bear
  only Dwarf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  tip Dismiss the leopard. Ice Claw Bears (level 7-8) roam the hills around Kharanos, many south-east of it and more north-west toward Anvilmar; their Ice Claw hits hard, so start at full health.
  kill 1196 quest 6085.1 "Tame Ice Claw Bear" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living bear
  turnin 6085                                 -- Grif Wildheart: Tame Beast
  accept 6086

step Belia Thundergranite in Ironforge
  only Dwarf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  zone Ironforge
  tip Belia Thundergranite, the pet trainer, stands in the Hall of Arms in Ironforge's Military Ward, by the hunter trainers.
  turnin 6086                                 -- Belia Thundergranite: Beast Training

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Night Elf: Dazalar in Dolanaar

step Dazalar in Dolanaar
  only NightElf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  zone Teldrassil
  tip At 10 go to Dazalar, the hunter trainer in Dolanaar. The Hunter's Path from Ayanna Everstride at Aldrassil, Jocaste in Darnassus, Einris Brightspear in Stormwind, Olmin Burningbeard in Ironforge or Grif Wildheart in Kharanos also leads here, for a little experience; it is only a pointer. In Elwynn at 10 instead? Josephine Carson's chain in Goldshire teaches the same.
  level 10
  accept 6063                                 -- Dazalar: the first Taming Rod

step Webwood Lurker
  only NightElf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  tip Webwood Lurkers (level 5-6) creep through the woods just north-east, south-west and east of Dolanaar. How the rod works: target a living beast, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you; moving, attacking it or anyone else's help breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges (out of charges: destroy the rod, abandon the quest, take it again). Their Web roots you but does not break the channel if you keep still. Keep each rod: it goes back to Dazalar.
  kill 1998 quest 6063.1 "Tame Webwood Lurker" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living spider
  turnin 6063                                 -- Dazalar
  accept 6101

step Nightsaber Stalker
  only NightElf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  tip Dismiss the spider first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet): a released practice pet can turn on you. Nightsaber Stalkers (level 7-8) lie on the hillside south of Lake Al'Ameth, south of Dolanaar; the plain Nightsabers by the village do not count.
  kill 2043 quest 6101.1 "Tame Nightsaber Stalker" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living stalker
  turnin 6101                                 -- Dazalar
  accept 6102

step Strigid Screecher
  only NightElf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  tip Dismiss the cat. Strigid Screechers (level 7-8), owls, perch in the woods south, south-west and west of Dolanaar.
  kill 1996 quest 6102.1 "Tame Strigid Screecher" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living owl
  turnin 6102                                 -- Dazalar: Tame Beast
  accept 6103

step Jocaste in Darnassus
  only NightElf
  when !onquest 94792,94863,94864,94793
  when !turnedin 94792
  zone Darnassus
  tip Take the road west from Dolanaar to Darnassus. Jocaste stands inside the Cenarion Enclave with the hunter trainers; Silvaria, the pet trainer, is up the ramp next to her.
  turnin 6103                                 -- Jocaste: Beast Training

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Goldshire (Human, Skyborne, or a Dwarf or Night Elf who took it there): Josephine Carson

step Josephine Carson in Goldshire
  only Human,Skyborne
  zone Elwynn Forest
  skipto pet when turnedin 94013
  tip At 10 go to Josephine Carson, the hunter trainer who stands with the other trainers by the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire; Isaac Chan, the pet trainer, is beside her. Skyborne: this is for one who left Zephras Isle without taming; it teaches the same.
  level 10
  accept 94792                                -- Josephine Carson: the first Taming Rod
  label goldshire

step Rockhide Boar
  when !turnedin 6064
  when !turnedin 6063
  tip Rockhide Boars (level 7-8) graze in three herds south and south-east of Goldshire, toward the Maclure Vineyards. How the rod works: target a living beast, use the Taming Rod and stand still for the whole channel while it hits you. Moving, fighting back, a heal from someone else or anyone else hitting the beast breaks it and costs one of the rod's few charges; if they run out, destroy the rod, abandon the quest and take it again. The boars use Rushing Charge, so start with the rod, not Auto Shot. Killing a boar does not count. Keep each rod: it goes back to Josephine. A Dwarf or Night Elf who took Josephine's rod instead of their home trainer's is led through Goldshire from here.
  kill 524 quest 94792.1 "Tame Rockhide Boar" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living boar
  turnin 94792                                -- Josephine Carson
  accept 94863

step Gray Forest Wolf
  when !turnedin 6064
  when !turnedin 6063
  tip Dismiss the boar first (right-click the pet portrait, Dismiss Pet): a released practice pet can turn on you. Gray Forest Wolves (level 7-8) run in the woods east of Goldshire, east of Crystal Lake.
  kill 1922 quest 94863.1 "Tame Gray Forest Wolf" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living wolf
  turnin 94863                                -- Josephine Carson
  accept 94864

step Young Forest Bear
  when !turnedin 6064
  when !turnedin 6063
  tip Dismiss the wolf. Young Forest Bears (level 8-9) roam the woods just south of Goldshire, with more south-west and south-east of town.
  kill 822 quest 94864.1 "Tame Young Forest Bear" -- Use the Taming Rod on a living bear
  turnin 94864                                -- Josephine Carson: Tame Beast
  accept 94793
  turnin 94793                                -- Isaac Chan, beside her: Beast Training

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Your own pet

step Your first pet
  label pet
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Tame Beast works like the rod: a beast of your level or lower, a channel you must not move during, the beast hitting you all the while. A pet keeps the level you tame it at and levels up with you; it can never be above your level, so tame one close to yours. Each family has its own ability on Forever (a boar's Charge, for example). For levelling, a cat hits hardest (Claw and Bite) and a boar takes more punishment.
  task "Tame a beast of your level to keep" optional
  note "Near Goldshire there are no cats: Prowlers (wolves, level 9-10) roam eastern Elwynn, Longsnouts (boars, 10-11) its far south-west by the Westfall border; at 12-13, Young Goretusks (boars) graze the fields of northern Westfall." only Human
  note "Near Kharanos: Snow Leopards (cats, level 7-8) prowl all over Dun Morogh, Scarred Crag Boars (9-10) its east toward Loch Modan; at 10-11, Mountain Boars roam western Loch Modan." only Dwarf
  note "Near Dolanaar: Elder Nightsabers (cats, level 8-9) and Feral Nightsabers (cats, 10-11) prowl the woods of north-western Teldrassil." only NightElf
  note "Near Valanaar: Vuldren Alphas (level 10), the beast of your last practice tame, hunt the Gustberry Lowlands; Shriekling Matriarchs (raptors, level 9) nest just west of Valanaar; Shadowgale Urseras (bears, 10-11) roam the north of Zephras Isle." only Skyborne
  note "Feed Pet: open your spellbook, cast Feed Pet and click a food your pet's family eats (the pet's tooltip lists them: cats eat meat and fish, boars almost anything). Raw meat looted from beasts counts. To buy: Toddrick the butcher in Goldshire, Jaeana in Darnassus and the innkeepers on Zephras Isle sell meat; the innkeepers of Kharanos and Dolanaar sell bread. Food near the pet's level makes it happiest; much lower food gives about half. You cannot feed in combat."
  note Happiness: the face on the pet frame. An unhappy pet does three quarters of its damage, a happy one a quarter more. Happiness drains slowly, faster when the pet dies; a pet left unhappy too long can run away.
  note Loyalty grows with time and kills. Each loyalty rank raises the training points you spend in Beast Training (pet level times loyalty rank minus one).
  note Beast Training (spellbook, General tab) teaches your current pet the abilities you know. To learn a new ability or rank: leave your pet with a stable master (Erma in Goldshire, Shelby Stoneflint in Kharanos, Seriadne in Dolanaar, Genn Fairweather on Zephras Isle), tame a beast that has it (its pet spellbook tab shows what it knows), use the ability in fights until the game says you learned it, then take your own pet back and teach it with Beast Training. A pet holds four active abilities at most.
  note Pet trainers sell Growl ranks and resistances. Alliance: Isaac Chan in Goldshire, Karrina Mekenda by the hunter trainers in Stormwind's Dwarven District, Peria Lamenur in Kharanos, Belia Thundergranite in Ironforge's Hall of Arms, Keldas in Dolanaar, Silvaria in Darnassus' Cenarion Enclave, Quel'dora Quickgale in Valanaar.
  note Call Pet, Dismiss Pet and Revive Pet are in your spellbook now; Mend Pet comes from your trainer at 12. A dead pet needs Revive Pet; one that is away more than about 100 yards is dismissed and comes back with Call Pet.
